{
  "analysis": "The zone size 600000 is likely hex (0x600000 = 6MB), which is correct. The real issue is Z_Malloc being asked for 25,145,144 bytes (~24MB), which exceeds the 6MB zone. This is likely an interpreter bug causing incorrect computation. I need to find the Z_Malloc address, add tracing, and inspect R_InitTextures to find where this bad size comes from.",
  "plan": "Find the Z_Malloc symbol address, inspect R_InitTextures source for allocation patterns, and add tracing to the VM to log Z_Malloc calls with the requested size. This will help identify whether the 25MB value is due to an interpreter bug.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "readelf -s /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -E \"Z_Malloc|R_InitTextures|R_InitData\" | head -10\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '300,460p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/r_data.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"Z_Malloc: failed\\|failed on allocation\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/z_zone.c | head -5\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
